## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- D8 adds the read-only, user-level public-profile foundation. Its only public
  database door is `public.profilo_pubblico(p_user_id uuid)`, backed by a closed
  seven-column projection in `private.profili_pubblici`.
- The public allowlist is exactly user UUID, username, bio, city, province,
  experience and avatar reference. D8 does not expose email, date of birth,
  roles, moderation internals, certification/trust data, metadata, future
  columns or the superseded `seller_verificato` semantic.
- Visibility reuses decision 7.6b: a removed target is absent, a removed
  authenticated caller reads no public profile, and a suspended user remains
  visible. Hidden and nonexistent UUIDs have the same zero-row response.
- D8 introduces no client `SELECT` on `profiles` or
  `profile_certifications`, no base-table RLS/grant relaxation and no general
  people directory. The RPC is `STABLE`, `SECURITY DEFINER`, has an empty
  `search_path`, returns at most one row and is executable only by `anon` and
  `authenticated`.
- `PublicProfileService` is server-compatible, rejects malformed UUIDs before
  PostgreSQL, maps database failures to application messages, reuses the
  fail-closed avatar sanitizer and reads active listings separately from the
  existing `public_listings` projection. A profile exists with zero listings.
- The D8 foundation verification measured **31 pass / 0 fail / 97 assertions**
  in the targeted service suite and **829 pass / 0 fail / 17673 assertions** in
  the then-complete `frontend-next` suite with Bun 1.3.14. The D8 UI Core raised
  that to **835 pass / 0 fail / 17705 assertions**. Public Profile Identity &
  Entry Points adds 28 tests: the stable complete-suite count measured twice with
  Bun 1.3.14 is **863 pass / 0 fail / 17793 assertions across 54 files**, and the
  CI `MIN_TESTS` floor plus the `prelaunch-contract` regression assertion are
  aligned to **863**.
- The D8 PostgreSQL 17.10 disposable grid applied all 38 migrations and produced
  **16 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**, with zero user, profile, role or audit residues
  after rollback. It was not executed against production.
- PR #87, `D8 Public user profile data foundation`, was merged into `main` at
  `73d5c7bf857f8bcfee387cf0ee4da2c2513be9e7`; its post-merge CI completed
  successfully. The D8 data/security foundation is CLOSED.
- PR #88, `Add D8 public profile UI core`, was merged into `main` at
  `3de888e5c6b5409492707f4be71d4e02be0750de`, verified on the remote default
  branch. The D8 Public User Profile UI Core is CLOSED; the route
  `/profilo/[id]` and its service are reused, not rebuilt.
- The avatar foundation (`risolviAvatarPersona` / `AvatarPersona`, photo →
  preset → silhouette, fail-closed) and the listing preview reused by the
  profile (`WineCard` list variant over `public_listings`) were already
  implemented before this work package and were reused unchanged.
- Production project ref is `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej`. Inclusion of migration
  `20260825180000 public_profile_foundation` in the production ledger remains
  **DA VERIFICARE**; the merge alone does not prove its application.
- The payout scheduler repository gate remains fail-closed and external Price
  Intelligence providers, KYC/identity providers, SMTP and payments remain OFF.

## ACTIVE TASK

### Public Profile Identity & Entry Points — VERIFY & SHIP

- Branch `d8-public-profile-entry-points`, cut from `origin/main` at
  `3de888e5c6b5409492707f4be71d4e02be0750de`, which had not advanced at verify
  time. No migration, schema, RLS or production write.
- Independent verification found and corrected one real defect: the listing
  seller card still ended its avatar chain on `inizialiDa()`, which the closed
  avatar foundation had already demoted — the documented order is photo →
  preset → silhouette. The card now draws `AvatarPersona`. Because
  `Wine.venditore.avatar` is an already recomposed URL, and feeding a URL back
  to the resolver would silhouette even a genuine photo, `rigaAWine` now also
  carries `venditore.avatarRef`, the safe reference produced by
  `riferimentoAvatarSicuro`. The pre-existing `venditore.avatar` contract and
  its `listing-avatar.test.ts` proof are unchanged. No new avatar logic, query
  or projection was introduced.
- `rigaProprietarioAWine` deliberately carries no `avatarRef`: its row has no
  seller UUID and adding one would mean widening a projection. The owner's own
  preview therefore falls to the silhouette instead of the broken relative
  `<img>` it drew before — fail-closed, and still not a public entry point.
- Listing detail, Messaggi and Club now reach `/profilo/[id]` using identifiers
  the read models already carried: `public_listings.seller_id`,
  `ConversationSummary.counterpart.userId`, `ClubPost.autoreId`,
  `ClubPostRisposta.autoreId` and `Club.ownerId`. No new query, projection or
  public-profile service was created.
- `Wine.venditore.userId` is optional. `rigaAWine()` fills it from `seller_id`;
  the demo `wines` data leaves it absent, so mock sellers produce no link
  instead of an invented profile. The owner's own preview
  (`rigaProprietarioAWine`) also leaves it absent and is not an entry point.
- `seller_verificato` is neither read nor reinterpreted by the new links; the
  professional-badge semantic stays out of scope and does not decide whether a
  profile is reachable.
- `ConversationHeader` and `ConversationList` now draw the counterpart avatar
  through `AvatarPersona` with `proprietarioId = counterpart.userId`, replacing
  a raw `<img>` over the client-writable `profiles.avatar_url`. The header
  carries the profile links; the list stays a selector with no nested
  interactive markup. The linked-listing image and link were already correct and
  were left untouched.
- Verification measured **28 pass / 0 fail** in
  `src/lib/profilo/ingressi-profilo-pubblico.test.ts`, full `frontend-next` lint
  at **0 errors / 11 warnings** — every warning pre-existing on `origin/main`,
  with one `<img>` warning removed net — a clean `tsc --noEmit`, a successful
  `bun run build` and a clean `git diff --check`. Browser smoke, DB grid,
  backend and payout runs were deliberately not executed.
- The pre-existing untracked `.wslconfig` remains excluded and untouched.

